#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-health-management-information-sy-0a3f5b.md:6
msgid "Automated data import from other systems. The HMIS should provide standard interfaces for the automated import of data from other systems, including the LHR and the PHSP, using agreed data standards such as ADX and FHIR, prioritising derivation from data already captured at the point of care over parallel reporting from health workers. (HMISF-4)"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-f-404ba5.md:3
msgid "Automated structural validation versus expert review in Monitoring. In the Monitoring category (and throughout release validation), governance rules must explicitly distinguish automated structural validation from expert semantic, clinical, policy, safety, and implementation review. Automated validation — such as schema and profile conformance checks, canonical URI and dependency integrity, value-set expansion verification, concept-map structural checks, and automated staleness or drift detection — is essential for verifying formal syntactic and structural constraints consistently at scale, but it cannot establish clinical appropriateness, semantic equivalence of translations or mappings, legal or ethical acceptability, patient safety, or real-world usability. Continuous SGI monitoring must therefore combine automated structural checks with periodic and event-triggered expert semantic, clinical, classification/coding, policy, legal, patient-safety, and implementation review, using field uptake telemetry and implementer feedback to detect semantic drift, unsafe coding patterns, or usability barriers in deployed systems."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-f-79f600.md:18
msgid "Automated Validation and Expert Quality Assessment"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-logical-information-model-reposi-257cac.md:25
msgid "Availability and performance. The LIMR shall be available to consuming systems for design-time model retrieval and runtime validation with sufficient reliability and performance to support its use as a shared reference asset across the health ecosystem, accepting that design-time access will typically be less latency-sensitive than the runtime terminology operations served by the TS."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-lifelong-health-record-131537.md:10
msgid "Availability and resilience. Design for high availability and continuity of access, ensuring that authorised users can retrieve critical health information at the point of care even under conditions of intermittent connectivity or partial system failure, including support for offline operation and synchronisation where required."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-lifelong-health-record-ed5e15.md:29
msgid "Availability and resilience. The LHR shall be designed for high availability, ensuring that authorised users can access critical health information at the point of care under conditions of intermittent connectivity, partial system failure, or planned maintenance, with defined recovery time and recovery point objectives commensurate with the clinical criticality of the information held."
msgstr ""

