#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-e-b1992f.md:5
msgid "Boundary of registry data, privacy compliance, and purpose-limited reuse: the Health Workforce Registry must comply with national data confidentiality, privacy, and data-protection laws. Detailed HR administrative records (such as extended leaves of absence, internal administrative or disciplinary proceedings, performance appraisals, and pay/deduction schedules) are held in employer HRIS and payroll systems; the shared registry records only the resulting high-level operational deployment status and regulator-issued licence/authorisation status. To prevent unnecessary exposure of personal residential addresses, nationality, disciplinary histories, salary details, or employment terms during payroll validation or workforce planning, the architecture enforces purpose-specific datasets and role-based access controls, provides de-identified or aggregated datasets for workforce planning and NHWA reporting, and gives health workers audit transparency into access to their records together with formal mechanisms for correction and appeal."
msgstr ""

