#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-e-b1992f.md:4
msgid "Care-services discovery model and dual national/international terminology governance: linking workforce and service delivery requires more than joining a worker identifier to a facility identifier. The mapping aligns the Health Workforce Registry, Health Facility Registry, and Terminology Service with a full care-services discovery model — such as the IHE Mobile Care Services Discovery (mCSD) profile — capturing the distinct relationships among Organisation (employer, regulator, or provider organisation), Practitioner (regulated or non-regulated worker), PractitionerRole (role, specialty, authorised scope of practice, task-sharing authority, contract/FTE basis, and active period), Location / Facility, and HealthcareService. Because international classifications alone cannot represent country-specific cadres, multiskilled workers, community health work, task sharing, or local scope of practice, the Terminology Service governs national occupation, role, specialty, credential, and scope-of-practice vocabularies separately and maintains structured mappings to international classifications — ISCO-08 (WHO health worker classification framework) for occupations and ISCED (International Standard Classification of Education) for educational qualifications — alongside interoperability with multi-source national data (regulatory registers, censuses, labour force surveys, and pension schemes) to populate NHWA indicators across licensed to practise, professionally active, and practising statuses."
msgstr ""

