#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-product-registry-2e4f9b.md:8
msgid "Does not assign or own product identifiers. Does not hold canonical product identity data. The catalogue it produces should trace every product entry to a Product Registry record — the management tool enriches and extends registry data, it does not replace or duplicate it."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-benefits-package-registry-distinguishing-the-benefits-pack-c66f4f.md:8
msgid "Does not author the canonical national definition of what benefit packages exist (that is the BPR's role). Does not hold canonical person, facility, workforce, or product identity records (those sit in the core DPI-H registries). Does not replace foundational payment settlement rails or public financial management systems."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-benefits-package-registry-distinguishing-the-benefits-pack-c66f4f.md:8
msgid "Does not define what benefit packages exist (that is the BPR's role). Does not manage provider contracts, tariffs, or claims adjudication (that is the CBMS's role). Does not replace the canonical health identity record in the Client Registry."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-benefits-package-registry-distinguishing-the-benefits-pack-c66f4f.md:8
msgid "Does not enrol individuals or store person-level membership. Does not execute person-specific eligibility determinations. Does not manage provider empanelment, payer-provider contracts, or negotiated fee schedules. Does not execute prior authorisation, adjudicate claims, assess service-delivery evidence, or initiate payments."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-product-registry-2e4f9b.md:8
msgid "Does not hold pricing, formulary status, therapeutic substitution rules, clinical indications, drug interaction data, procurement terms, or any attribute that is health-sector specific, operationally dynamic, or programme-dependent."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-benefits-package-registry-distinguishing-the-benefits-pack-c66f4f.md:6
msgid "Does not reference individual person records in the Client Registry. Publishes scheme and benefit definitions at the population category level — which schemes exist and what general criteria define eligibility — without recording individual enrolment."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-f-46b1ae.md:8
msgid "Domain authority (clinical specialty society, public-health programme authority, national classification centre, or regulatory agency): defines authoritative domain semantics, clinical appropriateness, classification conventions, and business rules for the affected domain, working alongside the programme owner who is accountable for programme indicators and service-delivery alignment."
msgstr ""

