#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-product-registry-2e4f9b.md:6
msgid "Dynamic. Operational attributes change regularly — prices are renegotiated seasonally or per procurement cycle, formulary decisions change with policy reviews, clinical guidance is updated with evidence. The catalogue is designed to accommodate this cadence."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-business-services-components-public-health-surveillance-platf-fe9ea4.md:2
msgid "Early detection of emerging threats through the application of configurable detection algorithms and statistical methods to routine surveillance data, identifying unusual patterns, clusters, and threshold exceedances that may signal the onset of an outbreak or other public health emergency before it becomes clinically apparent at the population level."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-public-health-surveillance-platf-181696.md:11
msgid "Early warning"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-health-facility-registry-7b0aec.md:1
msgid "Effective health service delivery, financing, and planning all depend on knowing where health facilities are, what they do, and whether they are operational. Without a reliable, interoperable health facility registry, every system in the health ecosystem maintains its own local version of the facility list — and those lists may diverge. For example, a logistics management system may route supplies to facilities whose identifiers do not always match the claims system's provider identifiers; there may be difficulty in attributing a case report to the correct administrative unit because its facility list references a district that was divided in a prior period; and health system managers may face challenges reimbursing services at facilities whose operational status has not been updated since the last manual audit."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-d-1-lifelong-health-record-3ef48b.md:2
msgid "EHRbase — an open-source, openEHR-conformant clinical data repository that stores and queries health data against openEHR archetypes and templates. \\cite{ehrbase}"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-benefits-package-registry-d6c531.md:6
msgid "Eligibility criteria and reference rule definition. The Benefits Package Registry shall support the formal definition and publication of general population-level eligibility criteria for each benefit package — including demographic, socioeconomic, employment-status, disease-specific, and geographic criteria — expressed as structured, testable machine-readable rule artefacts that consuming operational systems (such as a Beneficiary Registry, CBMS, or a separate governed rules service) can evaluate at runtime without the registry itself executing individual eligibility determinations."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-benefits-package-registry-d6c531.md:6
msgid "Eligibility criteria publication · Beneficiary enrolment support (FISF-01)"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-benefits-package-registry-d6c531.md:14
msgid "Eligibility criteria publication · Cross-sector coordination"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-business-services-components-public-health-surveillance-platf-fe9ea4.md:4
msgid "Elimination of parallel surveillance data collection by drawing on clinical data already held in the LHR, aggregate data from the HMIS, and person and facility references from the shared registries, reducing the reporting burden on health workers and facilities that would otherwise be required to submit the same data through multiple surveillance channels simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-health-workforce-registry-f926bd.md:18
msgid "Employment status"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-e-37b7cf.md:9
msgid "Enable patients, facilities, payers, and regulators to trust that a practitioner's registration, licence, or authorisation status is current — preventing payroll fraud and unsafe or uncredentialed care — while protecting worker privacy and labour rights."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-f-79f600.md:27
msgid "Enable search, browse and catalogue navigation of published artefacts"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-business-services-components-computable-decision-support-engi-2a67bd.md:2
msgid "Enabling timely ecosystem-wide updating of clinical guidance, so that when a guideline is revised the updated logic is available to all consuming applications without requiring each to be individually updated."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-benefits-package-registry-ad83df.md:7
msgid "End users of benefit entitlements. Access benefit definitions through beneficiary-facing portals, health wallets, and assisted-access channels that pair the registry's machine-readable definitions with plain-language, multilingual, accessible explanations."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-d-2-united-kingdom-england-a7ab86.md:1
msgid "England governs pharmaceutical decision support centrally — providing interaction checking, allergy alerting and dosage guidance to prescribing systems across primary and hospital care — and operates a national terminology service hosting the SNOMED CT UK Edition and the dictionary of medicines and devices. It demonstrates how centrally governed pharmaceutical knowledge and terminology can be deployed through standardised interfaces to a diverse ecosystem of consuming systems, reducing duplicated maintenance and improving consistency of medication-safety guidance."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-b-f241d4.md:5
msgid "Ensure quality and continuity of care"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-e-37b7cf.md:5
msgid "Ensure the right number and skill mix of trained health and care personnel are equitably distributed and retained across subnational areas and levels of care to meet population health needs, tracking NHWA licensed to practise, professionally active, and practising stock and inflows/outflows across the health labour market."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-d-1-public-health-surveillance-platf-92708e.md:6
msgid "Epi Info — a public-domain epidemiological analysis suite used in field epidemiology and ad hoc outbreak investigation. \\cite{cdc-epi-info}"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-public-health-surveillance-platf-181696.md:5
msgid "Epidemic preparedness"
msgstr ""

