msgid "Ministry of Health (package steward); health financing analysts and planners; scheme regulators; operational eligibility and claims systems (consuming reference definitions via API); beneficiary-facing portals and assisted-access channels."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-lifelong-health-record-ed5e15.md:11
msgid "Mixed structured and unstructured data. The LHR shall support the receipt and storage of clinical data that contains both structured and unstructured elements, accommodating the varying levels of data granularity that exist across contributing systems and care settings. (SHRF-4)"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-health-facility-registry-be234e.md:1
msgid "Mobile and temporary facility management. Support for facilities that operate temporarily, move location, or are established for specific campaigns or emergencies — including vaccination posts, emergency field hospitals, and mobile clinics — with full lifecycle management (activation, relocation, deactivation) and explicit linkage to the permanent facilities or organising entities responsible for them. Temporary facility records are distinct from permanent records and should be managed accordingly, including retrospective preservation of the services delivered and populations served during their active period."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-client-registry-307c48.md:1
msgid "Model A — HUID linked to national ID or CRVS. Where a robust foundational ID system exists, the HUID is derived from or permanently linked to the foundational identifier. The Client Registry stores the linkage and uses the foundational ID as the primary identity proofing source. This reduces duplication and strengthens the accuracy of identity resolution."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-logical-information-model-reposi-085ded.md:1
msgid "Model authoring and lifecycle management. Support for creating, versioning, reviewing, approving, deprecating, and retiring logical information models through defined governance workflows involving both clinical and technical stakeholders, with full version history, lifecycle states (draft, active, deprecated, retired), and traceability of changes over time."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-f-46b1ae.md:18
msgid "Model authority (technical modeller / steward)"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-client-registry-307c48.md:2
msgid "Model B — HUID not linked to national ID. Where a foundational ID system is absent, unreliable, or inaccessible to the health sector, the health system creates its own functional identifier independently. The Client Registry is the authoritative source for this health-specific identifier and manages its own identity proofing processes."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-client-registry-307c48.md:3
msgid "Model C — Multiple local health IDs linked through an EMPI. Where multiple facilities or programmes have each assigned their own local identifiers to the same population, the Client Registry functions as an Enterprise Master Patient Index — maintaining a cross-reference map that links these local identifiers to a single canonical person record."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-logical-information-model-reposi-257cac.md:4
#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-logical-information-model-reposi-257cac.md:5
#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-logical-information-model-reposi-257cac.md:6
#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-logical-information-model-reposi-257cac.md:21
#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-logical-information-model-reposi-257cac.md:22
msgid "Model governance"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-logical-information-model-reposi-257cac.md:3
msgid "Model Storage and Lifecycle Management"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-logical-information-model-reposi-257cac.md:4
msgid "Model storage and versioning. The LIMR shall store logical information models with full version history, supporting concurrent versions, lifecycle states (draft, active, deprecated, retired), and traceability of all changes over time, including the actor, timestamp, and reason for each change."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-health-facility-registry-8da585.md:4
msgid "Modelling of service coverage by planners against population distribution."
msgstr ""

