#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-benefits-package-registry-distinguishing-the-benefits-pack-c66f4f.md:7
msgid "Operational runtime. Active throughout every transaction cycle — enrolment, provider empanelment, contracting, pre-authorisation, claims submission, evidentiary review, adjudication, payment instruction, audit, and dispute resolution.Example: A provider submits a claim; the CBMS verifies provider empanelment and contract tariffs, evaluates the claim and supporting service-delivery evidence against adjudication rules, and issues an authorised payment instruction to payment rails."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-benefits-package-registry-distinguishing-the-benefits-pack-c66f4f.md:7
msgid "Operational runtime. Queried and updated during enrolment, point-of-care eligibility verification, and claims validation to confirm that a specific individual is actively enrolled in the relevant scheme and within their benefit limits.Example: A provider queries the Beneficiary Registry (via the CBMS or an eligibility service) at point of care to confirm that the patient is actively enrolled before rendering a covered service."
msgstr ""

