#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-health-workforce-registry-bbe9d8.md:1
msgid "Other considerations are that patients want to be assured that they are receiving care from practitioners whose registration status or licence can be verified at the point of service, health system managers want to know that fraud in payroll and insurance claims can be detected when provider identity can be confirmed, and ministries of health want to be able to make workforce planning decisions on reliable data, to address shortages and ensure distribution of the health workforce relative to population need. The WHO reports that the lack of sufficient health workers was consistently the most common cause of disruptions to essential health services, including during health emergencies like COVID-19 — a finding that depends on the kind of reliable workforce data that a functioning registry can provide (WHO NHWA handbook, Second Edition, 2023)."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-business-services-components-public-health-surveillance-platf-377702.md:5
msgid "Outbreak detection and early warning. Application of configurable detection algorithms, statistical thresholds, and spatial analysis methods to incoming surveillance data — contextualised against baseline trends from the HMIS — to identify unusual patterns, clusters, or threshold exceedances that may signal the onset of a public health emergency, with timely, structured alert generation to responsible authorities."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-public-health-surveillance-platf-181696.md:11
msgid "Outbreak detection and early warning. The PHSP shall apply configurable detection algorithms, statistical thresholds, and spatial analysis methods to incoming surveillance data, contextualised against baseline trend data from the HMIS, to identify unusual patterns, clusters, or threshold exceedances that may signal the onset of a public health emergency, generating timely, structured alerts with sufficient information to support rapid verification and response decisions."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-public-health-surveillance-platf-181696.md:10
msgid "Outbreak Detection and Response"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-business-services-components-computable-decision-support-engi-97cc2b.md:10
msgid "Override and justification capture. Mechanisms for authorised users to override or dismiss a recommendation with a documented reason, supporting clinical autonomy while maintaining accountability for departures from evidence-based guidance and enabling retrospective analysis of override patterns as a quality improvement feedback mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-computable-decision-support-engi-4b7f45.md:26
msgid "Override and justification capture. The CDSE shall allow authorised users to override or dismiss a recommendation and shall require the recording of a reason, supporting clinical autonomy while maintaining accountability for departures from evidence-based guidance. Override data shall be retained in a structured, reportable format to support retrospective analysis and knowledge governance."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-computable-decision-support-engi-4b7f45.md:27
msgid "Override pattern reporting. The CDSE should support the aggregation and reporting of override patterns to authorised governance bodies and, where appropriate, to the HMIS, enabling systematic review of decision support performance, identification of rules requiring refinement, and evidence-based improvement of the clinical knowledge base."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-business-services-components-benefits-package-registry-2f494f.md:7
msgid "Package lifecycle and version management. Maintenance of full version history for benefit package definitions, with support for concurrent versions, defined lifecycle states, and backward-compatible referencing so that operational claims systems can validate retrospective claims against the package version in effect at the time of care."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-product-registry-9abc28.md:4
msgid "Packaging hierarchy and unit of measure management. Definition and maintenance of the packaging levels for each product (unit, inner pack, case, pallet) with the associated GTINs and quantity conversions across levels, enabling consistent unit-of-measure handling across ordering, warehousing, and dispensing."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-product-registry-900dbb.md:17
msgid "Packaging hierarchy level"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-product-registry-7b92fe.md:6
msgid "Packaging hierarchy management. The Product Registry shall support the definition and maintenance of packaging hierarchies for each product, capturing the GTIN, unit of measure, and quantity conversion factor for each packaging level (unit, inner pack, case, pallet)."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-f-79f600.md:18
msgid "Pair automated structural, schema, and reference validation with expert semantic, clinical, classification, policy, safety, and implementation review"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-client-registry-a1d132.md:21
msgid "Parent-child and birth relationship management. The Client Registry shall support the persistence of parent-child relationships, birth order, and multi-birth indicators, linking child records to the mother's or guardian's canonical record and maintaining the relationship over time. (OpenHIE CRF-10)"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-benefits-package-registry-ad83df.md:5
msgid "Participating institution in multi-payer systems. May author and manage definitions for their schemes; queries public package definitions for coordination and anti-duplication."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-lifelong-health-record-ed5e15.md:15
msgid "Patient summary. The LHR shall support the retrieval of a patient summary — a structured overview of all clinically significant information known about a patient, with links to retrieve individual data items — enabling a provider encountering a patient for the first time to quickly establish clinical context. (SHRF-5d)"
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-e-37b7cf.md:6
msgid "Pay health and care workers accurately, reliably, and on time in compliance with labour rights, eliminate ghost workers and payroll leakage, and inform reporting on NHWA indicators on expenditure for compensation, entry-level wages and salaries, and pay gaps."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-benefits-package-registry-d6c531.md:8
msgid "Payer and scheme attribution. The Benefits Package Registry shall capture the payer or funding source responsible for each benefit package, including the identity of the administering institution, the financing mechanism, and the contractual or regulatory basis under which the package is offered, supporting multi-payer and mixed public-private financing environments."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-benefits-package-registry-distinguishing-the-benefits-pack-c66f4f.md:5
msgid "Payer-provider contracts and provider empanelment records (referencing the Health Facility and Health Workforce Registries); negotiated tariffs, fee schedules, and payment methods; premium and contribution schedules; executable pre-authorisation and claims adjudication rules; claims submissions, evidentiary assessments, adjudication outcomes, dispute records, and payment instructions."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-e-deab37.md:11
msgid "Payment decisions and financial controls versus payment settlement rails. Foundational payment DPI, banking interfaces, and treasury rails initiate, settle, and reconcile monetary transfers, but they do not determine whether a payment is accurate, lawful, contractually compliant, or appropriately authorised. Decisions on benefit coverage, claim validity, provider contract compliance, and financial control sit in operational health-financing, PFM, budget, contract, attendance, and payroll systems, which authorise payments before instructing payment rails to move funds and which govern timely health-worker and provider remuneration beyond DPI-H."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-metadata-registries-and-foundati-health-workforce-registry-c279d9.md:3
msgid "Payroll and incentive payment systems can use it to validate worker eligibility before disbursement."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-computable-decision-support-engi-4b7f45.md:33
#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-health-management-information-sy-0a3f5b.md:33
#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-supplier-registry-b00675.md:27
