#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-c-business-services-components-computable-decision-support-engi-2a67bd.md:3
msgid "Separating clinical knowledge governance from application development, enabling clinical experts and guideline developers to govern the content of decision support logic independently of the technical teams that build and maintain point-of-care applications."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/p-f-46b1ae.md:14
msgid "Separation of duties requires that the content author, technical modeller, or terminology specialist who drafts an artefact cannot act as its sole independent reviewer, domain approver, or publisher; for each artefact type, authoring is separated from independent review, domain/regulatory approval is separated from semantic/technical conformance sign-off, and final publication authority is exercised only after all required approvals are recorded."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/appendix/t-c-business-services-components-computable-decision-support-engi-4b7f45.md:13
msgid "Separation of logic and presentation. The CDSE shall deliver decision support outputs in a structured, machine-readable format independent of any specific user interface, so that consuming applications can present recommendations in a manner appropriate to their own workflow, without the CDSE prescribing how its outputs are displayed or acted upon."
msgstr ""

